{
  "delta_from_prior": "Upgraded from the 12-variable 128-clause skip fixture (auto_00051, which triggered no_dimension_reduction) to a 16-variable 408-clause width-8 UNSAT fixture where pinned v3 ACCEPTS compression (16 vars -> 12 vars, 408 clauses -> 102 clauses, certificate verified, automatic Lean check eligible) yet the compressed quotient STILL exhibits peak 32 residual growth under SCC-E-MRA+IALH-5. Unlike auto_00051, this separates residual search growth from BLQ discovery failure.",
  "explanation": "### 1. Code-Path Audit of Pinned v3 (`blq-localcert-scc-emra-ialh5-v3`)\n\nAuditing `compression.py` and `run_counting` for soundness bugs yields **no wrong-SAT defect**:\n- **Dense ID mapping & normalization**: `run_counting` normalizes the input before `compress_root`, stripping tautologies/duplicates; `_verify_certificate` checks `cert['variables'] == ids` and maps `ids` bijectively to `1..n` via `dense_formula`, rejecting any clause with duplicate/complementary literals (`len(set(map(abs, c))) != len(c)`).\n- **Quotient partition & local identity coverage**: `block_clause_counts` partitions every quotient clause across `sorted(blocks.items())` (`sum(counts) == len(quotient)`). For each block `(support, clauses)`, `forms[i] & ~mask == 0` ensures every quotient coordinate `i` used by `q` depends solely on `support`. Checking `evaluate(clauses, x) == evaluate(q, image)` across all `2**len(support)` points proves `clauses(X) == q(P(X))` for every global `X`; conjunction gives `original(X) == quotient(P(X))`.\n- **Right inverse & surjectivity**: `right_inverse` computes $L$ via GF(2) Gauss-Jordan elimination on `[P | I_r]`, and `_verify_certificate` independently checks every entry `parity(form & column) == int(i == j)` ($P L = I_r$), establishing surjectivity and equisatisfiability without $2^n$ or $2^r$ loops.\n- **Exact fallback & arithmetic**: Any failed budget, odd-block saturation, incompatibility, or rejected certificate falls back to `run_counting_core(formula, order)`. `refute` verifies every dual certificate via exact `Fraction` arithmetic, and `UNKNOWN` never returns SAT.\n- **Total solver work & greedy incompatibility**: Caps (`max_variables=64`, `max_block_width=8`, `max_clauses=1024`, `max_space_points=16384`, `max_verification_work=8000000`) bound preprocessing cost, not residual search. Greedy basis selection can still miss compatible bases (`incompatible_greedy_basis`), and\u2014crucially\u2014**even when compression succeeds completely, residual search can still blow up**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Construction: 16-Variable, 408-Clause Compressed-Quotient Growth Fixture\n\nRather than repeating a discovery skip (like the 88-clause incompatible case or `auto_00051`'s `no_dimension_reduction`), we construct a 16-variable UNSAT formula $F$ that **v3 genuinely compresses** (`16 -> 12` variables, `408 -> 102` clauses) while the **accepted quotient** still hits **peak 32**.\n\n#### Step A: 12-variable rigid UNSAT quotient $Q$ (102 clauses, width 6)\nPartition quotient variables `1..12` into four interleaved triples:\n- $A = \\{1, 5, 9\\}$, $B = \\{2, 6, 10\\}$, $C = \\{3, 7, 11\\}$, $D = \\{4, 8, 12\\}$,\nwith parities $p_A = y_1 \\oplus y_5 \\oplus y_9$, $p_B = y_2 \\oplus y_6 \\oplus y_{10}$, $p_C = y_3 \\oplus y_7 \\oplus y_{11}$, $p_D = y_4 \\oplus y_8 \\oplus y_{12}$.\n\nTake the 96 base clauses of `auto00007` across the 6 block supports $A\\cup B, C\\cup D, A\\cup C, B\\cup D, B\\cup C, A\\cup D$, encoding the UNSAT 2-CNF:\n$$(p_A \\lor p_B) \\land (p_C \\lor p_D) \\land (\\neg p_A \\lor \\neg p_C) \\land (\\neg p_B \\lor \\neg p_D) \\land (\\neg p_B \\lor \\neg p_C) \\land (\\neg p_A \\lor \\neg p_D).$$\nTo each of the 6 blocks, add **1 non-duplicate point clause** (forbidding one point outside the 16 base forbidden points):\n1. Block $A\\cup B$: `[-1, 5, 9, -2, 6, 10]` ($p_A=1, p_B=1$)\n2. Block $C\\cup D$: `[-3, 7, 11, -4, 8, 12]` ($p_C=1, p_D=1$)\n3. Block $A\\cup C$: `[1, 5, 9, 3, 7, 11]` ($p_A=0, p_C=0$)\n4. Block $B\\cup D$: `[2, 6, 10, 4, 8, 12]` ($p_B=0, p_D=0$)\n5. Block $B\\cup C$: `[2, 6, 10, 3, 7, 11]` ($p_B=0, p_C=0$)\n6. Block $A\\cup D$: `[1, 5, 9, 4, 8, 12]` ($p_A=0, p_D=0$)\n\nEach block of $Q$ now has **17 forbidden points (odd)**, so its translational stabilizer in $\\mathbb{F}_2^6$ is trivial ($\\{0\\}$). Adding clauses preserves UNSAT.\n\n#### Step B: Essential 4-variable XOR lift to 16 variables (408 clauses, width 8)\nSubstitute $y_9 = x_9 \\oplus x_{13}$, $y_{10} = x_{10} \\oplus x_{14}$, $y_{11} = x_{11} \\oplus x_{15}$, $y_{12} = x_{12} \\oplus x_{16}$, keeping $y_i = x_i$ for $1 \\le i \\le 8$.\n- Each width-6 clause of $Q$ touches exactly two lifted variables, expanding to $2^2 = 4$ clauses of width 8.\n- Each of the 6 blocks of $F$ has support width **8** ($\\le 8$) and $17 \\times 4 = 68$ clauses (64 base + 4 lifted outlier clauses), totaling **408 clauses** ($\\le 512$).\n- All 16 variables are essential to UNSAT; `space = 6 * 256 = 1536 <= 16384` and `verification_work` $\\approx 1.07 \\times 10^6 \\le 8 \\times 10^6$.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Exact Trace: Discovery Succeeds, Residual Search Still Blows Up\n\n1. **BLQ Compression (`compress_root`)**:\n   - All 6 blocks have 68 forbidden points (**even**), so `frozen` is empty.\n   - Because each 17-point quotient block has trivial stabilizer, the exact stabilizer of each 68-point lifted block is the 4-element kernel of its two lifted pairs, e.g., $\\text{span}(e_9 \\oplus e_{13}, e_{10} \\oplus e_{14})$ for $A\\cup B$.\n   - Its annihilator is $\\text{span}(e_1, e_2, e_5, e_6, f_9, f_{10})$ where $f_{8+j} = e_{8+j} \\oplus e_{12+j}$.\n   - In `candidates`, the 8 unit vectors $e_1, \\dots, e_8$ each have block count 3 and popcount 1, so they are selected first as quotient variables `1..8`. Next, among count-3 popcount-2 vectors, $e_1\\oplus e_5, \\dots, e_4\\oplus e_8$ are linearly dependent and skipped, while $f_9, f_{10}, f_{11}, f_{12}$ are independent and selected as quotient variables `9..12`.\n   - `chosen` has rank $12 < 16$, spans every block's annihilator (100% compatible), has an explicit GF(2) right inverse, passes `verify_certificate`, and outputs `quotient == Q` in ascending order `[1..12]`.\n2. **Residual Search (`run_counting_core(Q, [1..12])`)**:\n   - **Zero-Constraint Hull Lemma**: Any proper affine sublattice of $\\mathbb{Z}^k$ intersects $\\{0,1\\}^k$ in at most $2^{k-1}$ points (pair $\\{0,1\\}^k$ along a coordinate with nonzero coefficient mod $m$). Hence any window $w$ of size $k \\le 5$ with $> 2^{k-1}$ surviving UP tuples yields **zero** equalities or congruences in `hull_rows`.\n   - **Depths 0\u20134** (branching on `1, 2, 3, 4`, one per triple): At depth 0, all clauses have width 6 (`windows` is empty). By depth 4, every block has width 4 with 4\u20135 forbidden points (11\u201312 surviving tuples $> 8 = 2^3$), and any pairwise block union has size $\\ge 6 > 5$. Thus `refute` produces **0 constraints** (`UNKNOWN`), `canon_plus` finds 0 units/SCCs, and `elim_plus` accepts 0 eliminations (every variable has $\\ge 6$ pos and $\\ge 6$ neg occurrences). The 16 assignments to `(1,2,3,4)` induce distinct parity shifts, so none subsumes another: **16 states retained at depth 4**.\n   - **Depth 5** (branching on `5` $\\in A$): Blocks $A\\cup B, A\\cup C, A\\cup D$ shrink to width 3 (5\u20136 surviving tuples $> 4 = 2^2$), and pairwise unions of size 5 retain $\\ge 22 > 16 = 2^4$ tuples. Thus `refute` still produces 0 constraints, `elim_plus` accepts 0 eliminations, and **all 32 states survive at depth 5 (`peak = 32`)**.\n\nThis cleanly separates **discovery failure** (absent here: v3 compresses `16 -> 12` and qualifies for Lean verification) from **residual search growth** (peak 32 on the compressed quotient).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Critique of Fable's `auto_00057` Proposals (`LQC-GF2`, `FR-kappa`, `T94`/`T95`)\n\n1. **`LQC-GF2` (C1\u2013C4) and `T94`**: Removing the $2^{c_K}$ local table loop via cardinality check $m_K = |Q_K| \\cdot 2^{c_K - d_K}$ (requiring sorted duplicate-free $P_K, Q_K$) scales certificate *checking* to wider blocks, but our fixture already passes v3's local-table compression and still hits peak 32. Scaling verification does not bound residual search.\n2. **`FR-kappa` ($2^{e_K}$ per block)**: Fable claims `FR-kappa` mitigates incompatibility on even blocks while failing on odd blocks. Our fixture is a **reproducible counterexample** to parity-based expectations: **all 6 blocks have even size 68**, yet once the 4 lifted pairs are factored out, the residual 17-point blocks are rigid/odd and `FR-kappa` cannot collapse them further (and on higher excess dimension $e_K$, its $2^{e_K}$ clause blowup degrades total work).\n3. **Padding lemma & `T95`**: Fable's own padding lemma concedes extra-clause robustness is NP-hard, and solving adapted-basis discovery (`T95`) leaves our fixture untouched because v3 already finds the exact global quotient basis.\n\n---\n\n### 5. One Falsifiable Improvement & First Missing Theorem\n\n- **Falsifiable improvement (not raising caps)**: **Subformula-UNSAT BLQ relaxation**. Before falling back on odd/rigid blocks, greedily drop up to $\\delta$ outlier clauses per block (e.g. $\\delta \\le 4$ or 1 coset) to maximize stabilizer dimension, forming a relaxed subformula $F_{\\text{sym}} \\subseteq F$. If `compress_root(F_sym)` succeeds and `run_counting_core` proves $Q_{\\text{sym}}$ **UNSAT**, return **UNSAT** (sound because $F \\models F_{\\text{sym}}$); if $Q_{\\text{sym}}$ is SAT, discard it and run the exact solver on $F$. This collapses our 16-variable fixture (and `96+6`, `36+9`) from peak 32 to **peak 0**, and is immediately falsifiable by instances where the outlier clauses are *necessary* for UNSAT (making $F_{\\text{sym}}$ SAT).\n- **First missing theorem**: For general polynomial SAT (the barrier exposed here), neither `T94` (compositional verifier) nor `T95` (basis discovery) suffices; the first missing theorem is a **post-compression residual state-count bound** (or a sound non-affine cut/learning extension to `SCC-E-MRA + IALH-k`) bounding retained states polynomially on rigid quotients whose local windows satisfy $|T_w| > 2^{|w|-1}$.",
